  "summary_en": "Australia's consolidated Civil Aviation Safety Regulations 1998 (compilation of 29 September 2026), a comprehensive binding aviation safety regime administered by CASA. Only the table of contents is shown. Embodied-AI relevance is mainly Part 101 (unmanned aircraft and remotely piloted aircraft) and Part 47 (RPA registration), covering licensing, operator certification, registration and operating limits.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Part 101 regulates unmanned aircraft, RPA, model aircraft and rockets, including hazardous operation prohibition and visual line of sight rules",
   "RPA categories (micro, very small, small, medium, large) with remote pilot licences, RPA operator certification and accreditation",
   "Part 47 requires registration of certain RPA",
   "Part 101 prohibits launch or release of autonomous aircraft without approval (reg 101.097)",
   "Airworthiness certification, maintenance, and CASA approvals, exemptions and directions framework"
